      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pump_back_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "French traders made early European contact in the Pump Back area during the early eighteenth century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pump_back_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Salina Pumped Storage Project, known locally as the Pumpback, was developed in the late sixties as an experimental power project.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pump_back_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Grand River Dam Authority created the Pumpback to meet escalating electricity demands across northeastern Oklahoma.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pump_back_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Reversible pump-turbines at the Pumpback move water between Lake Hudson and the Holway Reservoir to generate electricity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/pump_back_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Pumpback facility can generate up to two hundred sixty megawatts of electricity during peak demand periods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
